[{"source": "acceptance", "severity": "warning", "category": "documentation", "title": "PR body omits the required [E10] citation (AC 3 enumerates it explicitly)", "location": "_bmad-output/pr-bodies/5.11.md", "evidence": "grep -o over the PR body: \"2 E31 / 2 E9.1 / 1 ODN-11 / 2 ODN-5 / 2 ODN-7\" and grep -n \"E10\" _bmad-output/pr-bodies/5.11.md → 0 matches (it appears only in demos/terminal_types.dem:19: \"# [E10]).\"). The PR body's re-bless section discusses replay without the tag: \"- **Logs:** all **32 existing `.log.bin`** byte-verified — they differ from HEAD ONLY in the 8-byte catalog_hash header field (bytes 17-24).\"", "detail": "Acceptance criterion 3 requires the PR body to include citations \"[ODN-5] [ODN-7] [E10] [E31] [E9.1]\". Four of five are present; [E10] (replay determinism lock) is missing from the body — the substance is covered but the mandated citation is not.", "recommended_fix": "Add the [E10] tag to the PR body's re-bless/verification section (e.g. \"Replay byte-identical [E10] — all 32 logs byte-verified, fold-only\")."}, {"source": "acceptance", "severity": "note", "category": "test-hygiene", "title": "W9 failure message still hardcodes \"(2 = ceil_cap)\" after the per-type re-pin", "location": "core/demand_test.odin:599", "evidence": "core/demand_test.odin:599: testing.expectf(t, burst_ok, \"no per-tick burst beyond the ceiling (2 = ceil_cap) may occur\") — directly below the re-pinned per-type check: \"acc := u64(spawn_credit_accrue_milli(cat, s.topology.node_type[src_slot])) / ceil_cap := (acc + 999) / 1000 / if u64(n) > ceil_cap { burst_ok = false }\" with the comment \"the ceiling is ceil(cap) per type — host 2, campus 3\".", "detail": "The re-pinned burst ceiling is type-relative (content_host 2, campus 3), but the assertion's failure text still says the ceiling is 2 — a campus burst-3 violation would print a false rationale.", "recommended_fix": "Update the message to \"no per-tick burst beyond the per-type ceiling (host 2, campus 3) may occur\"."}]
